  "description": "The current Airflow DAG configuration (version\u202f1) defines a workflow named **example_dag**, stored in the file **/usr/local/airflow/dags/example_dag.py**. The DAG is described as \u201cAn example DAG for testing.\u201d, uses the **graph** default view, and is oriented left\u2011to\u2011right (LR). It runs on the **UTC** timezone with a cron schedule of **\u201c0 12 * * *\u201d**. Concurrency is limited to **16** parallel runs, and only **1** active run is allowed at a time. Catch\u2011up is disabled, the DAG is not paused on creation, and it is not a sub\u2011DAG. The overall timeout for a DAG run is **7200** seconds. Access control grants the user **admin** both **can_read** and **can_edit** permissions. The DAG carries the tags **example** and **test**, and includes a documentation markdown block:\n\n```\n## Example DAG\nThis DAG demonstrates a simple workflow.\n```\n\nDefault arguments set the owner to **airflow** and the start date to the epoch timestamp **1700000000**. Additional parameters contain a single entry\u202f\u2014\u202f`param1` equals **value1**.\n\nThe workflow consists of two tasks. The first, **task_a**, is a **PythonOperator** (module\u202f`airflow.operators.python`) with UI colors **#ffefeb** (background) and **#000000** (foreground). Its template field is `python_callable`. It is owned by **airflow**, will retry up to **2** times with a retry delay of **300** seconds, and forwards execution to **task_b** (`_downstream_task_ids`\u202f=\u202f[`task_b`]). The second task, **task_b**, is a **BashOperator** (module\u202f`airflow.operators.bash`) also styled with background **#ffefeb** and foreground **#000000**. Its template field is `bash_command`, which is set to `echo 'Hello world'`. The task does not depend on past runs (`depends_on_past: false`).",
  "reference_json": {
    "__version": 1,
    "dag": {
      "_dag_id": "example_dag",
      "fileloc": "/usr/local/airflow/dags/example_dag.py",
      "tasks": [
        {
          "_task_type": "PythonOperator",
          "_task_module": "airflow.operators.python",
          "task_id": "task_a",
          "ui_color": "#ffefeb",
          "ui_fgcolor": "#000000",
          "template_fields": [
            "python_callable"
          ],
          "owner": "airflow",
          "retries": 2,
          "retry_delay": 300,
          "_downstream_task_ids": [
            "task_b"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_task_type": "BashOperator",
          "_task_module": "airflow.operators.bash",
          "task_id": "task_b",
          "ui_color": "#ffefeb",
          "ui_fgcolor": "#000000",
          "template_fields": [
            "bash_command"
          ],
          "bash_command": "echo 'Hello world'",
          "depends_on_past": false
        }
      ],
      "_access_control": {
        "admin": [
          "can_read",
          "can_edit"
        ]
      },
      "_concurrency": 16,
      "_default_view": "graph",
      "_description": "An example DAG for testing.",
      "catchup": false,
      "dagrun_timeout": 7200,
      "default_args": {
        "owner": "airflow",
        "start_date": 1700000000
      },
      "doc_md": "## Example DAG\nThis DAG demonstrates a simple workflow.",
      "is_paused_upon_creation": false,
      "is_subdag": false,
      "max_active_runs": 1,
      "orientation": "LR",
      "params": {
        "param1": "value1"
      },
      "schedule_interval": "0 12 * * *",
      "start_date": 1700000000,
      "tags": [
        "example",
        "test"
      ],
      "timezone": "UTC"
    }
  }
